From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] ecm_interface: track the bridge MDB without qca-mcs

The NSS multicast front end asks qca-mcs for the bridge ports of a
group. Nothing attaches qca-mcs to the bridge, so the lookup fails and
routed multicast to a bridge is never accelerated.

Read the egress ports from the bridge itself, as the Linux snooper mode
already does, in the NSS front end too. When the bridge has snooping
off or no querier, br_dev_xmit() floods routed traffic to every
forwarding port, so return those ports for locally sent traffic.
Bridged traffic is then also delivered to the host, which an
accelerated flow cannot do, so it stays unaccelerated. Skip ports that
are not forwarding and bound the port list before it is written.

Refresh the multicast connections of a bridge on the switchdev events
for MDB entries, STP state, mrouter ports and the snooping toggle. The
bridge sends them for every port, offloaded or not.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
